<osm version="0.6" generator="dayhike-fixture">
  <!-- Ways back no harder than the hike (ADR-0076). Five separate networks,
       far apart, each a Summit Trail from a portal P up to a summit S by a
       switchback W: about 9.0 km + 10.6 km one way, graded as named.

       Scramble Trail (4001, hiking): the only shorter way from S to P is the
         5.6 km Scramble, a demanding_alpine_hiking path: the hike is retraced.
       Easy Descent Trail (4002, hiking): beside the same Scramble, a 7.7 km
         hiking path S - E - P between the same two Junctions: it is the way back.
       Ungraded Trail (4003, no sac_scale): the only shorter way back is the
         5.6 km Steep Cut, a demanding_mountain_hiking path: the hike is retraced.
       Ungraded Ridge Trail (4004, no sac_scale): the only shorter way back is
         the 5.6 km Ridge Path, a mountain_hiking path: it is the way back.
       Alpine Trail (4005, alpine_hiking): the only shorter way back is the
         5.6 km Alpine Cut, an alpine_hiking path: it is the way back. -->
